// Legislation: ELI 1.4 and Akoma Ntoso 1.0: the standards' constraints, their sample data and the links between them
//
// Generated by ../../crosswalk.py from crosswalk.json, sample.json and the model.json and sample.json of each
// standard. Edit those and regenerate, rather than this file.
//
// Each standard's labels and relationship types are prefixed: ELI 1.4 as eli__, Akoma Ntoso 1.0 as akn__. The links
// between them are not.
//
// The Consumer Protection (Amendment) Act, 2024 of the fictional jurisdiction zz, and the Consumer Protection Act,
// 2012 it amends, as the Akoma Ntoso sample marks them up and as ELI metadata, added here, publishes them: each act
// as a legal resource with an English expression and an Akoma Ntoso XML format, the article of the amending act that
// substitutes an article of the principal act, the National Assembly that passed the act, the National Council for
// Law Reporting that publishes it, and the concept of consumer protection it is about. Each ELI node is linked to the
// Akoma Ntoso node describing the same thing, and the act's Akoma Ntoso FRBR URIs are the ELI local identifiers of
// its work, expression and format. The ELI IRIs are fictional; the ELI sample's GDPR has no Akoma Ntoso counterpart
// and is not linked. ELI 1.4: The General Data Protection Regulation, Regulation (EU) 2016/679, as published in the
// Official Journal: its English and French expressions and their PDF and XHTML formats, three of its articles, the
// 2018 corrigendum and the consolidated version that includes it, and the Data Protection Directive 95/46/EC it
// repealed. Beside it are the Law Enforcement Directive (EU) 2016/680, adopted the same day, and Ireland's Data
// Protection Act 2018, which transposes the directive and ensures the implementation of the regulation. Subdivision
// types and versions come from an example table, as ELI leaves them to each publisher; the other concepts come from
// the EU authority tables and ELI's own. Akoma Ntoso 1.0: A fictional amending act, the Consumer Protection
// (Amendment) Act, 2024 of a fictional jurisdiction (country code zz, which ISO 3166 leaves to users), with its FRBR
// identification, publication, lifecycle, references, classification and the structure of its preamble and body down
// to articles, paragraphs and the people, terms and dates their text refers to. An article of the Act substitutes an
// article of the principal act, the Consumer Protection Act, 2012: the Act's analysis records it as an active textual
// modification with its source, destination and period, and the principal act, kept as a document of its own, records
// the same change as a passive modification.
//
// Run it against an empty database of Neo4j 5 or later, Enterprise Edition, for its node key and property existence
// constraints, e.g. with cypher-shell -f model.cypher. It merges every node and relationship, so it can be run again.

// The standards: their constraints

